<h2>1. WordPress core</h2>
<p><strong>Version:</strong> 6.4.2 → 6.5.1</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>ID / CVE</th><th>Title</th><th>CVSS</th><th>Affected range</th><th>Fixed in</th><th>Fixed by this update</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://www.wordfence.com/vulnerability/core-1" rel="noopener noreferrer">CVE-2024-0001</a></td><td>Vulnerability core-1</td><td>9.8 (Critical)</td><td>&gt;= 0 &lt; 6.5</td><td>6.5</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.wordfence.com/vulnerability/core-2" rel="noopener noreferrer">CVE-2024-0002</a></td><td>Stored XSS | in *comments* [x]</td><td>6.1 (Medium)</td><td>&gt;= 6.4 &lt;= 6.4.3, &gt; 6.5.1</td><td>6.5.1</td><td><span class="warn">⚠ no</span></td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-0003" rel="noopener noreferrer">CVE-2024-0003</a></td><td>Open redirect</td><td>4.3 (Medium)</td><td>&lt; 6.5.1</td><td>—</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">Sources: wordfence</p>
